WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:06.569
In this era of endless sequels, reboots, and
reunions, no successful screen property is

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:08.019
ever really complete.

00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:12.980
With television in particular, a big finale
doesn't necessarily spell the end anymore.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:18.600
Sometimes, it's a no-brainer that an ultra-popular
original series will get a spinoff, and once

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.100
it does, the follow-up becomes beloved in
its own right.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.730
But other times, audiences fall in love with
a promised spinoff, only to see it fizzle

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.680
out before it even debuts.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.530
Here are some of the TV spinoffs that never
quite made it to air.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.910
How I Met Your Dad

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.120
How I Met Your Mother attracted millions of
faithful viewers who stuck around for nine

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.719
seasons to find out the full story of how
Ted Mosby fell in love with his kids' mystery

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:45.719
mom.

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:49.600
The finale ended up disappointing plenty of
fans, but there was a chance to wash that

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.609
bad taste away with a spinoff that CBS ordered
in 2014.

00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:58.930
How I Met Your Dad was to star Greta Gerwig,
but CBS was unhappy with the first pilot and

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:01.840
unable to agree on conditions for a second.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.500
Casting and rights ownership issues were also
later cited as reasons the network preemptively

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.850
pulled the plug.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:09.850
The Farm

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:16.790
In 2012, as The Office's final season loomed,
NBC execs worked with Rainn Wilson to develop

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:20.860
a potential spin off centered around his character
Dwight Schrute.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:25.240
Entitled The Farm, it would focus on Dwight's
vegetable farm and bed and breakfast, and

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.670
all the strange figures in his personal life.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:33.921
"Growing up with Dwight and Mose, was not
easy, Dwight was obviously the cool one, and

00:01:33.921 --> 00:01:38.140
Mose was the visionary, which left me to be
the comedian"

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:40.950
Unfortunately, the network was unimpressed.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.390
Most of the scenes shot for the would-be backdoor
pilot made it into an episode of The Office's

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:50.920
last season, but NBC had already decided that
they wouldn't turn The Farm into a series.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.160
The Office may eventually return in some form,
however.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:59.780
In late 2017, reports surfaced that NBC was
again considering a way to revive the cult

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:05.960
favorite comedy with a new series featuring
a mix of returning stars and newcomers.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:06.960
Valley Girls

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:13.360
The CW's Gossip Girl was a very successful
teen soap opera, brimming with bonkers storylines

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.270
while also being tongue in cheek.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.140
At the height of its popularity during the
second season, the wheels started turning

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.840
on a potential spinoff called Valley Girls.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.530
The series would have launched with the second
season episode of the same name, which flashed

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:31.630
back to the teen years of Serena van der Woodsen's
mother Lily, as played by Brittany Snow.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:37.420
It was set in 1980s Los Angeles, instead of
Gossip Girl's cushy digs on Manhattan's Upper

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.420
East Side.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:43.170
The cast also featured Krysten Ritter as Lily's
sister, along with guest appearances from

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:46.300
No Doubt and '80s icon Andrew McCarthy.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:51.510
But shortly before the season 2 episode aired,
the CW quietly backed away from the spin-off

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.360
project.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.730
Aquaman

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.700
The long-running superhero series Smallville
followed Clark Kent's life in the title town

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.080
before he became Superman.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:06.130
It enjoyed strong viewership and featured
a cavalcade of supporting characters whose

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.250
lives and adventures could potentially be
explored further.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:14.510
A season 5 episode featuring Alan Ritchson
as A.C. Curry, a.k.a.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:19.850
Aquaman, inspired a potential standalone series
for the character, with actor Justin Hartley

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.230
taking over the role.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:26.720
The CW ultimately declined to pick up the
series, instead releasing the pilot as a standalone

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:27.720
feature.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.220
But it didn't work out so bad for Hartley,
as he later joined Smallville as Oliver Queen,

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.220
a.k.a.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.220
the Green Arrow.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:38.500
In 2018, Hartley revealed that there had also
been plans for a spinoff featuring himself

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.590
as Oliver and Erica Durance as Lois Lane.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:45.940
Instead, those characters remained on Smallville,
while a separate Green Arrow series later

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:49.460
premiered on The CW in 2012.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.750
The Chatterbox

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:55.890
With the possible exception of Steve Urkel,
no sitcom star's voice has ever been quite

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:58.630
as iconic as Fran Drescher's on The Nanny.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:03.180
She was at once charming and annoying, trashy
but still sophisticated.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:08.000
As the show became a hit and introduced several
characters from Fran's past, CBS was ready

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.460
to consider a spinoff.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:15.040
A backdoor pilot, entitled "The Chatterbox,"
aired late in The Nanny's second season.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:19.350
It took place at Fran's favorite hair salon
and introduced viewers to the new characters

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.380
who worked there.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.070
But despite some earnest efforts by the would-be
spinoff's cast members, The Chatterbox never

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.960
made it onto CBS's schedule.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.630
Assignment: Earth

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.960
There have been numerous versions of Star
Trek over the years.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.970
In fact, one of the earliest attempted spinoffs
happened near the beginning of the original

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:38.970
series' run.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:43.800
In the second season episode "Assignment:
Earth," actor Gary Lansing was introduced

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:49.820
as Gary Seven, a time-hopping alien on a mission
to save humanity with his trusty cat by his

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:50.820
side.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:51.970
"Computer, record the following.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.009
Unless agents are found immediately, must
undertake their mission"

00:04:56.009 --> 00:05:00.220
The episode was meant to serve as a backdoor
pilot, but the original series itself was

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:03.900
in danger of cancellation, so Assignment:
Earth was never picked up.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:09.020
But since then, there has been a seemingly
endless number of Star Trek remixes on the

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:11.590
silver, small, and now streaming screens.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:17.180
So despite this early setback, the franchise
has indeed gone on to "live long and prosper."

